# axial credentials — copy this file to .env and fill in only the keys you need.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and is read by `axial taxonomy` and `axial judge` from the
# repo root. Two rules worth knowing: a variable already exported in your shell
# always wins over this file, and an empty value here is skipped rather than set,
# so an unfilled placeholder can never mask a real export.
#
# Which keys you need depends on `judge_model` in .axial/config.toml.
# `axial init`, `ingest`, `sample`, `annotate`, `label-from-reviews`, `split`,
# `align`, `promote` and `gate` call no model at all and need nothing here.


# --- text models, reached through litellm ------------------------------------
# Required by `axial taxonomy` (it must write prose) and by `axial judge` when
# judge_model names a text model. The default judge_model is "claude-opus-5",
# which litellm routes to Anthropic.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Only if you point judge_model at an OpenAI model such as "gpt-5".
# OPENAI_API_KEY=


# --- decision models, reached through OpenRouter's Decisions API --------------
# Required by `axial judge` when judge_model is "typesafe/jev-1.13".
# Jev is not served on the chat-completions endpoint, so this key is separate
# from anything litellm uses — get it from https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
